Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** for `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

> **Integration-test calibration applied.** The class carries `[TestCategory("Integration")]`, so Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severities are evaluated against integration norms. All 19 catalog smells were checked; 15 returned clean.

---

## Findings by Severity

### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Smell:** `if`/`else` branch inside the test body means one path is never exercised for a given run; the assertion that runs depends on a runtime type check the test doesn't control.

**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` — lines 101-108

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // path A
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // path B
}
```

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Whichever branch never triggers is dead code — you have invisible zero coverage on one assertion path, giving false confidence.

---

### ❷ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Smell:** The test exercises code but makes no assertion. MSTest will report "Passed" as long as no exception is thrown, even if every insert silently fails.

**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` — lines 113-119

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

**Fix — verify the observable outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — the test will stay green even if `Insert` silently drops every record.

---

### ❸ Sleepy Test — **Medium** *(downgraded from High; integration context)*

**Smell:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces a hard 3-second wall-clock wait, making the suite slower and timing-dependent.

**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` — line 87

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);

Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead of sleeping:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll up to 5 s, succeed as soon as the notification arrives
    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5),
        interval: TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within the timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3 s of unconditional wait on every run. In CI under load the delay may be insufficient, causing flaky failures (Camara et al., SAST 2021 link to flakiness).

> *Severity note:* Downgraded from High because this is an integration test where some async coordination is expected. The smell is still real — the fix is to poll rather than sleep.

---

### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Smell:** Four consecutive assertions with no explanation messages. When one fails, the MSTest output shows only the assertion type and values, not *which property* was wrong.

**Location:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` — lines 35-38

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add message parameters:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** When a failure occurs in CI, the developer must open the source to determine which of four assertions failed — slows triage.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining **4 tests** are well-structured:

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert; 2 focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single `Assert.IsNull` — clean negative check |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | `Assert.AreEqual(3, ...)` is contextually obvious (3 inserts above) — not a Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async `await`, concise assertion on count |

The class also correctly uses `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` (no Constructor Initialization smell), in-memory SQLite (no Mystery Guest or Resource Optimism), and both fixture fields are used by every test (no General Fixture).

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** — `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after the loop | ~1 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | Split into two deterministic tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** — `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with a poll-with-timeout helper | ~10 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** — `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | Add message strings to each assertion | ~2 min |

Fix priorities 1 and 2 first — they are the only findings that can cause **silent false passes** (tests that report green while bugs exist). The Sleepy Test and Assertion Roulette findings affect maintainability and flakiness but don't mask bugs.
